# Effective ignore list for images built from the repository root, which is now
# the build context for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# Patterns without a wildcard prefix match only at the context root, so the
# nested forms below are required. Two of them are load-bearing:
#
#   **/node_modules  A local backend/node_modules holds a Prisma client
#                    generated for the developer's own platform. Copied into the
#                    image it would sit at /app/backend/node_modules and take
#                    resolution priority over the correctly generated hoisted
#                    client at /app/node_modules, producing an engine mismatch
#                    at runtime.
#   **/.env*         backend/.env contains DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET, and admin
#                    credentials. It must never be baked into an image layer.
#
# prisma/migrations/migration_lock.toml is deliberately NOT excluded: Prisma uses
# it to detect a provider mismatch between the migrations and the target
# database.

**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.gitignore
# Both the bare and nested forms are listed on purpose. `**/` is documented to
# match zero path segments, but a secret is not the place to depend on that.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/dist
**/.next
**/.cache
**/coverage
**/*.log

*.md
docs/

**/prisma/*.db
